18:T41b,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"If life is just God's 'play', why is there so much suffering?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In a drama or a video game, conflict, difficulty, and 'villains' make the game engaging. Suffering occurs because we forget we are actors playing a role, and we take our finite ego-character too seriously."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How does viewing the world as Lila change your perspective?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It shifts life from a grueling 'test' you must pass to an ecstatic dance to be enjoyed. You still perform your duties, but with a lightness of heart, knowing the outcome belongs to the Divine Game-Maker."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between Maya and Lila?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Maya is the mechanical illusion (the stage, the props, the costumes). Lila is the motivation (the joyous script being acted out by God). Maya bounds you; recognizing Lila frees you."}}]}10:["$","div",null,{"className":"min-h-screen bg-background text-foreground flex flex-col","children":[["$","$L17",null,{"slug":"lila","pillar":"sanskrit-lexicon"}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$18"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"DefinedTerm\",\"name\":\"Lila\",\"description\":\"Lila represents the joyous, spontaneous, and dramatic play of the Divine, offering a beautiful perspective that views the creation of the universe as an act of ecstatic cosmic sport rather than necessity.\",\"url\":\"https://opensadhaka.com/learn/sanskrit/lila\",\"inDefinedTermSet\":\"https://opensadhaka.com/learn/sanskrit\"}"}}],["$","$L19",null,{}],["$","main",null,{"className":"flex-grow pt-24 pb-16","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container-padding max-w-5xl mx-auto","children":[